. Gamuda Gardens is thoughtfully designed to be self-sustaining with a host of modern conveniences amongst nature, so residents can enhance their quality of life. There are five cascading lakes in the central park and the township is anchored by the waterfront retail village that offers cafes, restaurants, retail outlets, and other amenities to serve the needs of the communities. The word ‘GAIA’ means ‘Earth’ in Greek, which implies a living, breathing organism and giver of life. In line with Gamuda Land’s development philosophy of “listening to what the land has to tell you”, Gaia Residences is planned with landscaping and water features that blend seamlessly into Gamuda Gardens’ backdrop. The developer’s thoughtful preservation of the hills creates a sense of place as residents are able to have hillside homes or lakeside homes. Gaia Residences is designed to take advantage of the lush terrain at Gamuda Gardens, and thus, some of the units enjoy a view of the waterfall, hills and lakes that sit across the development. Gamuda Gardens is located at the northern end of Kuala Lumpur, putting it just a 5-minute drive away from the confluence of the Guthrie Corridor Expressway (GCE), LATAR Expressway, and North-South Expressway (NSE). From there, residents are connected to KL, and other townships and attractions. Guthrie Corridor Expressway (GCE) leads to Bukit Jelutong, and Shah Alam. North-South Expressway (NSE) leads to Kuala Lumpur city centre, Petaling Jaya, Subang Jaya, and Shah Alam. LATAR Expressway connects to Kuala Selangor, and Selayang. For public transport, there’s Kuang KTM Station (3km), MRT Sungai Buloh Interchange Hub and Sungai Buloh KTM Station (10km), and Rawang KTM Station (10.5 km). The GAIA Boulevard is an elevator ride away, and that means residents are minutes away from eateries, laundrette, and convenience stores. Residents may also take an e-scooter ride or board the shuttle bus that makes its rounds around Gamuda Gardens. There’s a host of amenities surrounding Gaia Residences, including: offers al-fresco styled retail experience, with an established grocery brand, a two-storey drive-thru and a wide selection of services, children enrichment centres, pharmacies and convenience stores. , which houses a FIFA-standard football field, where casual and professional-level games can be held. with a mix of local and international grocery, fashion, and F&B brands to satisfy residents’ retail cravings. There’s also a 50-acre pet-friendly Central Park and cascading lakes, and residents can also move around via eco-friendly scooters and bicycles. Additionally, the Fun Park at Gamuda Luge Gardens is just minutes away. Launched in 2018, GAIA Residences features 500 units across two towers of 18 storeys, with built-ups ranging from 550 to 900 sq ft. There’s also 18 units of two-storey shops, and 12 units of retail shops.\n\nRead more\n\nProject details\n\nType Service Residence\n\nPrice RM 203K - 448K\n\nCompletion year 2021\n\nTenure Leasehold\n\nNo. of blocks 1\n\nNo. of floors 18\n\nTotal units 500\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRumah untuk Dijual - Bawah RM  400K di GAIA Residences, Ogos 2026 (https://www.propertyguru.com.my/bm/hartanah-dijual/di-gaia-residences-18071/harga-dibawah-rm-400k)\nciteturn242search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; RM 380,000 RM 575.76 PSF GAIA Residences Lorong Serai, Bandar Gamuda Gardens, Rawang, Selangor 2 1 2 660 kps Servis Apartment Pegangan Pajakan Tahun siap: 2021 Disenaraikan pada 05 Ogo 2026 (1 hari lalu)Hubungi WhatsApp WhatsApp\n\n# 11 Rumah untuk Dijual - Bawah RM  400K di GAIA Residences\n\nTunjukkan Peta\n\n[Input]\n\n[Input]\n\nDesmond Lim\n\nImage: chevron-left-f\n\nImage: chevron-right-f\n\n14\n\nRM 202,700 RM 313.78 PSF GAIA Residences Lorong Serai, Bandar Gamuda Gardens, Rawang, Selangor 2 1 2 646 kps Servis Apartment Pegangan Pajakan Tahun siap: 2021 Disenaraikan pada 05 Ogo 2026